     "body": "Found while writing the masking docs (d153f0259).\n\nWith **Mask personal data** on, `postgres://app:hunter2pass@db.acme-corp.cn:5432/x` is masked as `app:{{EMAIL_…}}:5432`: the password and host become one EMAIL placeholder. With only **Mask secrets** on, the same text gives `{{PASSWORD_…}}` for the password and leaves the host, as intended.\n\nThe password still never reaches the vendor, but the kind is wrong and the host the model may need is hidden. A URL's userinfo should be judged before the email matcher takes `pass@host`.\n\nReproduced with the masking preview (Settings › Privacy › Try it) code path in a throwaway test; not yet fixed.",
     "reactions": {
