   "created_at": "2026-11-08T19:42:17Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T19:42:17Z",
   "body": "Correction to my earlier replies: saying that nothing ending in .local can be a mail address was too broad. An organisation can use a private mail domain, and current main deliberately preserves masking for local/internal/lan/corp and similar suffixes (mailTLD/localTLDs in internal/redact/redact.go).\n\nPlease do not apply my old branches' blanket .local exclusion as a general fix. It would leave a genuine private email address unmasked. The reported mDNS/SSH user@host form needs a contextual distinction from mail, rather than treating the suffix alone as proof.\n\nI checked that source contract at b1e8eb15. I have not established a complete context rule with both the original hostname examples and private-email positive controls, so I am withdrawing the earlier claim that those branches are ready as a privacy-safe resolution of this issue. No replacement patch or live gateway verification is claimed in this follow-up.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
